<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="{{ route('orbit.home') }}">Home</a><span>/</span>Journal</div><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT PLANNING</p><h1>Choosing a package by scope, not just by price</h1><p class="intro-text">The useful comparison is what will be delivered, what you need to supply and what sits outside the fee.</p></div><div class="intro-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></div></section><section class="section"><article class="container article-body"><p class="article-byline">OrbitIT editorial · Practical guidance</p><h2>Count deliverables</h2><p>A page design and a coded page are different deliverables. A content batch is different from ongoing social account management. Read the included items before comparing fees.</p><h2>Check the inputs</h2><p>Some packages assume you provide copy, images, branding or an existing platform. If these are not ready, agree additional preparation work rather than leaving the assumptions unclear.</p><h2>Separate external costs</h2><p>Domains, hosting, advertising spend, paid themes and platform fees are separate unless the written quotation says otherwise. Check the final total before agreeing to proceed.</p><h2>Make revisions specific</h2><p>Agree how feedback is consolidated, how many revision rounds are included and what counts as a change of scope. Clear boundaries help both the business and its service provider.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{ route('orbit.blog') }}">← Back to the journal</a></article></section><section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="cta-block"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT MOVE</p><h2>Good ideas deserve<br>a clear direction.</h2><p>Let’s turn what you have in mind into an agreed plan.</p></div><a class="btn btn-lime" href="{{ route('orbit.contact') }}">Tell us about your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
